1
00:00:00,245 --> 00:00:00,858
Hi there!

2
00:00:00,858 --> 00:00:03,050
Welcome to Shelfie.

3
00:00:03,953 --> 00:00:06,915
Lots of small food sellers still run on paper.

4
00:00:06,915 --> 00:00:08,090
A home baker.

5
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:09,503
A market stall.

6
00:00:09,503 --> 00:00:11,303
The menu is a printed sheet,

7
00:00:11,303 --> 00:00:13,003
and there's no website.

8
00:00:13,003 --> 00:00:15,903
AI assistants are starting to shop for people,

9
00:00:15,903 --> 00:00:18,303
but they can't see a paper menu.

10
00:00:18,303 --> 00:00:20,966
In one US survey, nearly half of food

11
00:00:20,966 --> 00:00:23,640
and lodging businesses had no website.

12
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:27,533
Shelfie gives them a shop that AI can buy from.

13
00:00:28,653 --> 00:00:29,953
It takes three steps.

14
00:00:29,953 --> 00:00:31,440
Snap your price list.

15
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:33,265
Let AI shoppers order.

16
00:00:33,265 --> 00:00:35,583
Get paid on PayPal.

17
00:00:37,962 --> 00:00:40,337
Meet Rosa, a home baker.

18
00:00:40,337 --> 00:00:42,687
She signs up with an email and a password,

19
00:00:42,687 --> 00:00:44,892
and adds her bakery.

20
00:00:45,845 --> 00:00:47,595
She snaps her price list.

21
00:00:47,595 --> 00:00:49,507
Claude, an AI model,

22
00:00:49,507 --> 00:00:53,125
reads every item and price in under ten seconds.

23
00:00:54,445 --> 00:00:56,770
Anything unclear becomes a question,

24
00:00:56,770 --> 00:00:59,520
like this two for seven dollars deal.

25
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:02,608
She adds her PayPal email and publishes.

26
00:01:02,608 --> 00:01:06,175
Each item lands in PayPal's catalog.

27
00:01:07,512 --> 00:01:10,112
Every shop also gets an agent door:

28
00:01:10,112 --> 00:01:12,112
one web address where any AI

29
00:01:12,112 --> 00:01:14,937
assistant can read the menu and order.

30
00:01:14,937 --> 00:01:18,942
It uses MCP, an open standard.

31
00:01:20,103 --> 00:01:21,753
Watch Claude Code try it,

32
00:01:21,753 --> 00:01:23,803
given only the shop's link.

33
00:01:23,803 --> 00:01:27,203
It finds the door by itself, orders two croissants,

34
00:01:27,203 --> 00:01:29,883
and hands back a PayPal link.

35
00:01:31,437 --> 00:01:34,549
Buyers can browse every shop on Shelfie.

36
00:01:34,549 --> 00:01:37,362
Each tap adds to the order, one switch flips

37
00:01:37,362 --> 00:01:41,342
to the assistant, and checkout goes to PayPal.

38
00:01:42,453 --> 00:01:44,640
Or they just ask the assistant.

39
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:47,091
This buyer has a nut allergy.

40
00:01:47,091 --> 00:01:49,378
Each step shows in plain words,

41
00:01:49,378 --> 00:01:51,753
with the details a tap away.

42
00:01:51,753 --> 00:01:54,991
It warns that the almond croissants contain nuts,

43
00:01:54,991 --> 00:01:57,783
and orders once they say yes.

44
00:01:59,087 --> 00:02:01,200
Payment happens on PayPal.

45
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,125
The buyer approves, and the money

46
00:02:03,125 --> 00:02:06,392
lands in Rosa's own PayPal account.

47
00:02:07,887 --> 00:02:10,437
The order pops up on Rosa's dashboard,

48
00:02:10,437 --> 00:02:11,912
already paid.

49
00:02:11,912 --> 00:02:13,937
Claude pulls it from PayPal and writes her

50
00:02:13,937 --> 00:02:17,592
a short brief, flagging the nut allergy.

51
00:02:18,887 --> 00:02:20,712
Prices stay hers, too.

52
00:02:20,712 --> 00:02:22,737
When an AI tries to pay one cent,

53
00:02:22,737 --> 00:02:24,792
the shop says no.

54
00:02:26,320 --> 00:02:28,120
The whole picture: Claude reads

55
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:30,257
the menu and writes the brief.

56
00:02:30,257 --> 00:02:32,182
PayPal holds the catalog,

57
00:02:32,182 --> 00:02:35,032
takes the payment, and pays the seller.

58
00:02:35,032 --> 00:02:38,483
The agent door lets any AI assistant order.

59
00:02:38,483 --> 00:02:41,775
A sheet of paper is all Rosa needed.

60
00:02:43,162 --> 00:02:45,242
Thanks for watching!
